I would like to invite the following historical figures to our party:

- Confucius (551 BC–479 BC), the Chinese philosopher and politician;
- Laozi (6th century BC), the traditional author of the Daodejing and one of the founders of Daoism; 
- King Wen of Zhou (c. 1250 BC), the last ruler of the Shang dynasty;
- King Wu of Zhou (c. 1100 BC), the first ruler of the Zhou dynasty.

While I'm not sure if they are all available, my goal is to have a great dinner conversation about their political experiences in China. However, I want to emphasize that King Wu was an antagonist and I don't plan on him joining me again.
